            <h2 class="mb-0">Feline Food</h2>
            <p style="max-width: 550px; margin:  0 auto;">
                Cats are cherished companions for millions of people
                worldwide. As cat owners, it's our duty to ensure they receive top-notch care, including providing
                them with nutritious cat food. Selecting the perfect cat food for your furry friend can be
                overwhelming, given the numerous products claiming to be the best. However, it's crucial to note
                that not all cat food is created equal. Some options may contain harmful ingredients or lack
                essential nutrients.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="row gy-4 align-items-center features-item" style="row-gap: 30px;">
            <div class="col-lg-5  order-1-class justify-content-center flex-column aos-init aos-animate"
                 data-aos="fade-up">
                <h3>
                    Raw Meat
                </h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <span>
                            Feeding your cat raw meat is undoubtedly the healthiest option, perfectly suited for
                            their carnivorous digestive system. This natural diet not only satisfies their predatory
                            instincts but also plays a key role in preventing and addressing various health issues.
                            Raw meat is the ultimate source of essential proteins, fats, and vitamins that may be
                            lost during the cooking process.
                        </span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span>
                            Embracing this natural feeding approach aligns with their ancestral diet, providing a
                            meal that is both instinctively appealing and beneficial for their overall well-being.
                            Cats, in their natural habitat, wouldn't think twice about grilling or frying their
                            catch before eating it. This highlights their innate preference for raw, unprocessed
                            meat, which best supports their biology. By choosing to feed them this way, we honor
                            their true nature and encourage a lifestyle that closely resembles their wild
                            experience, ensuring they thrive with vitality and good health.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                </ul>

            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-7 order-2-class d-flex align-items-center aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-out"
                 data-aos-delay="100">
                <div class="image-stack">
