<section class="testimonial-area  pb-5 pt-4">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="testimonial-wrapper-two">
            <div class="row no-gutters">

                <div class="col-lg-6 order-1-class">
                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column"
                         style="background-image: url(/webassets/images/bg/testimonial-bg-3.jpg); visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">
                        <div class="section-title section-title-left pb-1">
                            <span class="sub-title">Cons of Dry Food for Cats:</span>
                        </div>
                        <p style="border-left: 8px solid #ffd74e;
        padding-left: 16px;">
                            <b>Moisture Content:</b> The most critical issue with dry food is its low moisture
                            content. Cats
                            naturally have a low thirst drive and derive much of their water intake from their food.
                            A diet exclusively based on dry food can lead to dehydration and is often linked to
                            urinary tract diseases.
                        </p>

                        <p class="my-2" style="border-left: 8px solid #ffd74e;
        padding-left: 16px;">
                            <b>Carbohydrate Levels:</b> Dry foods typically contain higher levels of carbohydrates
                            than wet
                            foods. High carbohydrate intake can lead to obesity and diabetes, conditions
                            increasingly seen in domestic cats.
                        </p>
                        <p class="my-2" style="border-left: 8px solid #ffd74e;
                                padding-left: 16px;">
                            <b>Variability in Quality:</b> The quality of
                            dry food can vary significantly between brands. Some may use high levels of fillers and
                            low-quality ingredients that offer less nutritional value to your cat.
                        </p>
                        <p class="my-2" style="border-left: 8px solid #ffd74e;
                                                        padding-left: 16px;">
                            <b>Palatability:</b>While many cats
                            enjoy dry food, some may find it less palatable than wet food. This can especially be a
                            problem for picky eaters or cats with certain health issues that affect their appetite.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 order-2-class">
                    <img src="~/webassets/images/elements/step-38.jpg" alt="img" style="border: 4px solid red;">
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>
